            <ArticleTitle>Coronary embolism following aortic and mitral valve replacement: successful management with abciximab and urokinase.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>457-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of coronary embolism in a 63-year-old woman with St. Jude aortic and mitral valve replacements who presented with acute myocardial infarction. Urgent catheterization revealed a saddle embolus in the proximal part of the circumflex and ramus arteries and another embolus in a diagonal branch. After employing angioplasty for the totally occluding diagonal embolus, a combined regimen of intracoronary urokinase and intravenous abciximab was successful in achieving complete resolution of the emboli.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
